### P0-2: Animation Metadata System

**Status**: Not Started
**Effort**: Small (1-2 days)
**Dependencies**: P0-1
**Spec Reference**: User Architecture Overview → Metadata-Driven
**Status Reference**: STATUS-2025-12-08-052243.md §2.6 "React Gallery Architecture"

#### Description
Create TypeScript types and metadata file describing all 62 animations. This is the single source of truth for gallery rendering.

#### Acceptance Criteria
- [ ] `src/types/animation.ts` defines `Animation`, `Technique`, `Variant`, `Target` types
- [ ] `src/data/animations.ts` exports array of 62 animation metadata objects
- [ ] Metadata includes: id, technique, target, variant, filePath, title, description
- [ ] TypeScript enforces type safety (no `any` types)
- [ ] Metadata validates against actual file existence (script or test)
- [ ] Techniques grouped into categories matching current index.html sections
- [ ] Variants: "original", "varied", "procedural" correctly tagged

#### Technical Notes
```typescript
// Example type structure
type Technique =
  | 'line-drawing'
  | 'particles'
  | 'morphing'
  | 'glitch'
  | 'liquid'
  | 'kinetic'
  | 'transforms-3d'
  | 'reveal-mask'
  | 'wave-ripple'
  | 'typewriter';

type Target = 'logo' | 'text';
type Variant = 'original' | 'varied' | 'procedural';

interface Animation {
  id: string; // e.g., 'logo-01-line-drawing'
  technique: Technique;
  target: Target;
  variant: Variant;
  filePath: string; // relative to gallery root
  title: string;
  description: string;
  dynamicTextSupport?: boolean; // if has postMessage API
}
```

