### P1-3: State Management (MobX or Context)

**Status**: Not Started
**Effort**: Medium (3-5 days)
**Dependencies**: P0-2, P1-1
**Spec Reference**: User Architecture → State Management
**Status Reference**: STATUS-2025-12-08-052243.md §2.6 "React Gallery Architecture"

#### Description
Implement gallery state management for accordion collapse/expand, selected animation, parameter editor state.

#### Acceptance Criteria
- [ ] MobX store OR React Context + hooks implemented
- [ ] State includes: expandedSections (Set<Technique>), selectedAnimation (string | null)
- [ ] `toggleSection(technique)` action/function to collapse/expand sections
- [ ] `selectAnimation(id)` action/function to set active animation
- [ ] State persists during navigation (no page refreshes yet, but prepare for routing)
- [ ] TypeScript types for all state and actions
- [ ] No prop drilling (state accessible via context/observer)

#### Technical Notes
**Option A: MobX**
```typescript
class GalleryStore {
  expandedSections = new Set<Technique>();
  selectedAnimation: string | null = null;

  toggleSection(technique: Technique) {
    if (this.expandedSections.has(technique)) {
      this.expandedSections.delete(technique);
    } else {
      this.expandedSections.add(technique);
    }
  }
}
```

**Option B: React Context + useReducer**
```typescript
type GalleryState = {
  expandedSections: Set<Technique>;
  selectedAnimation: string | null;
};

type GalleryAction =
  | { type: 'TOGGLE_SECTION'; technique: Technique }
  | { type: 'SELECT_ANIMATION'; id: string };
```

**Recommendation**: Start with Context + useReducer (simpler, no dependencies), migrate to MobX if complexity grows.

