### P2-1: Track Class Implementation

**Status**: Not Started
**Effort**: Medium (3-5 days)
**Dependencies**: None (but resolve BLOCKER-2 first)
**Spec Reference**: User Architecture → Core Layers → Track
**Status Reference**: STATUS-2025-12-08-052243.md §2.4.2 "Level 1: Track"

#### Description
Implement core Track class with getValue(t), easing integration, and type-specific interpolation.

#### Acceptance Criteria
- [ ] `src/core/Track.ts` created in TypeScript
- [ ] Generic Track<T> class supports number, {x,y}, color, path interpolation
- [ ] getValue(t): returns interpolated value at time t
- [ ] Delay and duration respected
- [ ] Easing function applied correctly
- [ ] Unit tests: 100% coverage of Track class
- [ ] Tests validate: delay, duration, easing, interpolation correctness
- [ ] Benchmark: track overhead <1ms per getValue() call

#### Technical Notes
```typescript
class Track<T> {
  constructor(
    public from: T,
    public to: T,
    public duration: number,
    public delay: number = 0,
    public easing: EasingFunction = linear
  ) {}

  getValue(t: number): T {
    if (t < this.delay) return this.from;
    const localT = (t - this.delay) / this.duration;
    const progress = Math.min(1, localT);
    const eased = this.easing(progress);
    return this.interpolate(this.from, this.to, eased);
  }

  protected interpolate(a: T, b: T, t: number): T {
    // Type-specific interpolation
    if (typeof a === 'number') return lerp(a as number, b as number, t) as T;
    if ('x' in a && 'y' in a) return { x: lerp(a.x, b.x, t), y: lerp(a.y, b.y, t) } as T;
    // ... more types
    throw new Error('Unsupported interpolation type');
  }
}
```

