### P2-6: Animation Base Class

**Status**: Not Started
**Effort**: Medium (3-5 days)
**Dependencies**: P2-3, P2-4
**Spec Reference**: User Architecture → Core Layers → Animation
**Status Reference**: STATUS-2025-12-08-052243.md §2.4.4 "Level 3: Animation"

#### Description
Implement Animation base class with state machine (entrance/hold/exit/waiting), element management, and loop control.

#### Acceptance Criteria
- [ ] `src/core/Animation.ts` created
- [ ] State machine: 'entrance' | 'hold' | 'exit' | 'waiting'
- [ ] entrance(): starts animation, transitions to hold after entrance complete
- [ ] exit(): starts exit animation, transitions to waiting after exit complete
- [ ] restart(): resets to entrance state
- [ ] loop(): requestAnimationFrame-based update loop
- [ ] Elements: add/remove elements, update all elements per frame
- [ ] holdDuration, exitDuration configurable
- [ ] Unit tests: state transitions, loop control
- [ ] Integration test: create animation with 3 elements, verify lifecycle

#### Technical Notes
```typescript
class Animation {
  elements: AnimatedElement[] = [];
  state: 'entrance' | 'hold' | 'exit' | 'waiting' = 'waiting';
  private startTime: number = 0;
  private exitStartTime: number = 0;
  private loopId: number | null = null;

  constructor(
    public holdDuration: number = 2000,
    public exitDuration: number = 250
  ) {}

  entrance(): void {
    this.state = 'entrance';
    this.startTime = performance.now();
    this.loop();
  }

  exit(): void {
    this.state = 'exit';
    this.exitStartTime = performance.now();
  }

  restart(): void {
    // Hook for variant mode (resolve BLOCKER-2)
    if (this.onRestart) {
      const newConfig = this.onRestart();
      this.updateConfig(newConfig);
    }
    this.entrance();
  }

  private loop = (): void => {
    const t = performance.now() - this.startTime;

    if (this.state === 'entrance') {
      this.elements.forEach(el => el.update(t));
      if (this.isComplete(t)) {
        this.state = 'hold';
        setTimeout(() => this.exit(), this.holdDuration);
      }
    } else if (this.state === 'exit') {
      const exitT = performance.now() - this.exitStartTime;
      this.elements.forEach(el => el.updateExit(exitT));
      if (exitT >= this.exitDuration) {
        this.state = 'waiting';
        return; // Stop loop
      }
    }

    if (this.state !== 'waiting') {
      this.loopId = requestAnimationFrame(this.loop);
    }
  };

  private isComplete(t: number): boolean {
    // Check if all elements have completed entrance
    return this.elements.every(el => el.isComplete(t));
  }
}
```

---

### P2-7: Config Hot-Swap System (Resolve BLOCKER-2)

**Status**: Not Started
**Effort**: Medium (3-5 days)
**Dependencies**: P2-6
**Spec Reference**: ENGINE-FLEXIBILITY-ANALYSIS.md §1 "Variant-Specific Code"
**Status Reference**: STATUS-2025-12-08-052243.md §2.9 "Concern 1: Variant-Specific Code"

#### Description
Design and implement config hot-swap mechanism to support "varied" mode per-restart randomization without destroy/recreate cycles.

#### Acceptance Criteria
- [ ] AnimationHooks interface: onRestart?() => AnimationConfig
- [ ] Animation.updateConfig(partial): hot-swaps config without destroying elements
- [ ] Varied mode: onRestart generates new random config each restart
- [ ] No memory leaks from create/destroy cycles
- [ ] Performance: hot-swap <10ms (benchmark)
- [ ] Unit tests: config updates, hook invocation
- [ ] Integration test: varied animation restarts 10 times with different configs

#### Technical Notes
```typescript
interface AnimationHooks {
  onRestart?: () => Partial<AnimationConfig>;
}

class Animation {
  constructor(
    private config: AnimationConfig,
    private hooks?: AnimationHooks
  ) {}

  restart(): void {
    if (this.hooks?.onRestart) {
      const newConfig = this.hooks.onRestart();
      this.updateConfig(newConfig);
    }
    this.entrance();
  }

  updateConfig(partial: Partial<AnimationConfig>): void {
    Object.assign(this.config, partial);
    // Rebuild tracks for elements based on new config
    this.rebuildTracks();
  }

  private rebuildTracks(): void {
    // Update tracks for all elements without destroying elements
    for (const element of this.elements) {
      // Clear old tracks
      element.tracks.clear();
      // Add new tracks based on updated config
      this.addTracksForElement(element, this.config);
    }
  }
}
```

**For varied mode**:
```typescript
const animation = new Animation(config, {
  onRestart: () => ({
    colors: { hueShift: Random.range(-15, 15) },
    motion: { mode: Random.pick(['converge', 'cascade', 'diagonal']) }
  })
});
```

