### P2-13: Remaining Animation Factories (8 types)

**Status**: Not Started
**Effort**: XL (2+ weeks)
**Dependencies**: P2-6, P2-8, specialized elements
**Spec Reference**: User Architecture → Animation Factories (10 types total)
**Status Reference**: STATUS-2025-12-08-052243.md §2.1 "Complete Animation Type Analysis"

#### Description
Implement animation factories for remaining 8 techniques: morphing, glitch, liquid, kinetic, 3D transforms, reveal, wave, typewriter.

#### Acceptance Criteria
- [ ] createMorphingAnimation(): uses PathTrack for shape interpolation
- [ ] createGlitchAnimation(): uses NoiseTrack for jitter, multi-layer rendering
- [ ] createLiquidAnimation(): uses SVG goo filter, wobble tracks
- [ ] createKineticAnimation(): uses CSS transforms, radial entrance
- [ ] create3DTransformAnimation(): uses CSS 3D transforms (rotateX/Y/Z)
- [ ] createRevealAnimation(): uses SVG mask, position interpolation
- [ ] createWaveAnimation(): uses OscillatingTrack for sine wave motion
- [ ] createTypewriterAnimation(): uses StepTrack for discrete letter reveal
- [ ] Each factory has: config presets, unit tests, visual tests
- [ ] All 10 factories documented with examples

#### Technical Notes
**Morphing** (uses flubber.js or custom path interpolation):
```typescript
function createMorphingAnimation(
  container: SVGSVGElement,
  startPaths: PathData[],
  endPaths: PathData[],
  config: MorphingConfig
): Animation {
  const animation = new Animation(config.timing.holdDuration, config.timing.exitDuration);

  startPaths.forEach((startPath, index) => {
    const element = new PathElement(container, `morph-${index}`);
    const morphTrack = new PathTrack(
      startPath.d,
      endPaths[index].d,
      config.timing.duration,
      index * config.timing.stagger,
      easing.inOutCubic
    );
    element.addTrack('path', morphTrack);
    animation.addElement(element);
  });

  return animation;
}
```

**Wave** (uses OscillatingTrack):
```typescript
function createWaveAnimation(
  container: SVGSVGElement,
  elements: SVGElement[],
  config: WaveConfig
): Animation {
  const animation = new Animation(config.timing.holdDuration, config.timing.exitDuration);

  elements.forEach((el, index) => {
    const element = new TransformElement(el);
    const waveTrack = new OscillatingTrack(
      config.frequency,
      config.amplitude,
      index * config.phaseOffset,
      config.decayRate,
      config.timing.duration
    );
    element.addTrack('translateY', waveTrack);
    animation.addElement(element);
  });

  return animation;
}
```

