### P2-15: Performance Benchmarking

**Status**: Not Started
**Effort**: Medium (3-5 days)
**Dependencies**: P2-9, P2-10, P2-13
**Spec Reference**: README.md "Performance Considerations"
**Status Reference**: STATUS-2025-12-08-052243.md §2.9 "Concern 3: Performance Implications"

#### Description
Benchmark track-based animations vs original standalone files to validate performance (target: no regression, 60fps maintained).

#### Acceptance Criteria
- [ ] Benchmark suite: measure FPS, frame time, memory usage
- [ ] Test scenarios: line drawing (10 elements), particles (3000), complex (all 10 types)
- [ ] Baseline: original HTML files performance
- [ ] Track-based: new factories performance
- [ ] Results: <5% performance regression acceptable
- [ ] If regression >5%: identify bottlenecks, optimize
- [ ] Document: performance report with graphs
- [ ] Mobile device testing (iOS, Android)

#### Technical Notes
**Benchmark script**:
```typescript
// benchmark.ts
async function benchmarkAnimation(animation: Animation, duration: number = 5000): Promise<BenchmarkResult> {
  const frames: number[] = [];
  let lastTime = performance.now();

  animation.entrance();

  const measureFrame = () => {
    const now = performance.now();
    const frameDuration = now - lastTime;
    frames.push(1000 / frameDuration); // FPS
    lastTime = now;

    if (now - startTime < duration) {
      requestAnimationFrame(measureFrame);
    } else {
      const avgFps = frames.reduce((a, b) => a + b, 0) / frames.length;
      const minFps = Math.min(...frames);
      console.log(`Avg FPS: ${avgFps}, Min FPS: ${minFps}`);
    }
  };

  const startTime = performance.now();
  requestAnimationFrame(measureFrame);
}
```

**Chrome DevTools**: Use Performance tab to record, check for jank, long tasks.

